# for server/results/e1/, e2/, etc: those ARE committed — Chapter 4 is
# built from them and I7 alone isn't enough reason to keep a reader from
# seeing a number without re-running a 20-minute experiment. Path-anchored
# so it catches only the draft directory, not every "results" anywhere.
